## How to run

Use the commands in `docs/agent/LONGRUN.md` validation gates.

## Validation evidence

- UNCONFIRMED: record commands run before review freeze.
- UNCONFIRMED: record known failures and waived checks.

## Review lanes

Each reviewer works independently against the same frozen commit.

- security
- architecture
- tests
- UX / visual behavior
- performance
- maintainability

## Review report format

Write one JSON report per lane under:

```text
docs/reviews/pending/<lane>.json
```

Minimum shape:

```json
{
  "reviewer_lane": "security",
  "base_commit": "{{CURRENT_COMMIT}}",
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "SEC-001",
      "severity": "P1",
      "claim": "Describe the issue.",
      "evidence": {"files": ["src/example.ts:1"], "observed": "..."},
      "affected_files": ["src/example.ts"],
      "acceptance_criteria": ["Expected behavior is verified."],
      "validation_commands": ["npm test"],
      "requires_human_decision": false
    }
  ]
}
```

## Normalize feedback

After all reports are complete:

```bash
python scripts/normalize_reviews.py --target .
```

Then fix tickets from `docs/reviews/ReviewQueue.json` one at a time.
